        lines+=['','These are separate no-autocast FP32 and FP16 execution policies; they do not replace the primary AMP training comparisons. Only original_fp32 loads the original checkpoint. It is a dense-materialized reference of that original native function; its dense resident allocation is not the native training parameter residency. Source model tensor bytes, excluding optimizer state, are recorded independently. FP32-factor resident copies are counted; FP16-factor mode retains actual FP16 buffers. The training model has no KV cache, so every generated token recomputes its prefix. Context32/96,16tokens, greedy/teacherforced,20groups, equal warmup; fixed fresh-process ordering, finalD2H/hash excluded. Shared embedding/head, causal attention, positions, top2 routing/probabilities and complete SiLUup/down all execute. Correctness, every condition and traces remain linked.', 'Storage rounding ΔNLL in consistentFP32: `'+json.dumps(d['rounded_export_minus_original_fp32_nll'])+'`; directFP32 versus samepayload denseFP32: `'+json.dumps(d['direct_minus_same_payload_reference_nll'])+'`; directFP16 versus samepayload denseFP16: `'+json.dumps(d['direct_fp16_minus_dense_fp16_nll'])+'`. DirectFP16 versus originalFP32 additionally changes execution precision: `'+json.dumps(d['direct_fp16_minus_original_fp32_nll'])+'`.', 'Paired generation latency intervals: `'+json.dumps(d['comparisons'])+'`.',evidence(path/'native_runtime_results.json'),evidence(path/'payload_correctness.json'),'']
        bounds=d['direct_fp16_minus_dense_fp16_nll']['ci95'];latency=[r['direct_minus_dense_generation_seconds']['ci95'] for r in d['comparisons'] if r['precision']=='FP16'];equivalent=bounds[0]>=-.001 and bounds[1]<=.001
